  "problem": "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** the sun does not come out, **then** it does not get warmer.",
  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ The sun does not come out.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ It does not get warmer.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A\u21d2B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB\u21d2A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it does not get warmer, then the sun does not come out.",
